data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"I need to run npm install. Let me do that, then build and serve. Since the task needs me to verify the served interface, I'll need to run the dev server and then fetch/curl it or use a headless browser. Let me think about how to check the rendered page.\n\nI can install dependencies and build. Then run the serve command. To check the rendered interface, I can use curl or wget to fetch the HTML and maybe use a headless browser like puppeteer/playwright if installed. But that might be overkill. I can:\n1. npm install\n2. npm run build\n3. npm run serve (in background)\n4. curl the page to get HTML\n5. Check the source includes the expected elements\n\nBut the requirement says \"the rendered page contains elements with data-component=Header, data-component=Footer, and data-component=Button\". These are rendered by React client-side, so the initial HTML may not contain them. I might need to use a headless browser or check the JavaScript bundles. \n\nActually, since React 19 renders client-side, the `data-component` attributes will be in the DOM after hydration but not necessarily in the initial HTML response. I can use a tool like `curl` with JavaScript execution, or use `puppeteer`/`playwright` if available, or even use `node` with a headless browser.\n\nLet me first install dependencies and build. Then think about the verification method. I can use `npx playwright` or install it. Actually, simpler: I can use `curl` to fetch the page and the JS bundle, and grep for the data-component patterns in the bundle. But the task specifically says \"the rendered page contains elements with data-component=...\" which implies runtime DOM check.\n\nLet me check what's available. Maybe I can use Node with jsdom, or use a browser via puppeteer. Let me see if chromium/playwright is installed."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789849377,"id":"chatcmpl-d702ca55105b4eac998d44104b37785a","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

